1
00:01:30,540 --> 00:01:32,250
[MITHRIL]
Really?

2
00:01:32,330 --> 00:01:34,710
Anne, are you being serious?

3
00:01:34,790 --> 00:01:35,710
[ANNE]
Yes.

4
00:01:35,790 --> 00:01:37,670
Are you sure?

5
00:01:37,750 --> 00:01:40,460
But the crest of House Chamber
is supposed to be a taboo!

6
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:42,250
Do you have any idea?

7
00:01:43,750 --> 00:01:44,830
[MITHRIL]
Oh!

8
00:01:46,790 --> 00:01:48,580
Well, all right.

9
00:01:48,670 --> 00:01:51,580
Then I'll help you.
Need some pigment powder?

10
00:01:52,210 --> 00:01:54,330
Thank you.
I really appreciate it.

11
00:01:55,330 --> 00:01:59,000
I need purple, red, and blue
and green and black, as well.

12
00:01:59,080 --> 00:01:59,920
Leave it to me!

13
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,540
Oh, and everything
that's close, if you don't mind!

14
00:02:03,630 --> 00:02:04,750
Sure!

15
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:08,880
[ANNE] A crest is the pride
of a noble family.

16
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:11,380
And in Noah's eyes

17
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:12,630
the crest of House Chamber

18
00:02:12,710 --> 00:02:14,380
is almost like
Lord Herbert's spirit

19
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:15,670
in physical form.

20
00:02:16,580 --> 00:02:18,250
That's why he watches over it.

21
00:02:18,330 --> 00:02:20,670
♪

22
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:25,500
Even if the symbol is forbidden
it still matters to him.

23
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:27,920
He's been gazing at it
all this time!

24
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:32,170
♪

25
00:03:00,420 --> 00:03:02,920
♪

26
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,210
Is it done now?

27
00:03:10,630 --> 00:03:12,250
[ANNE]
Yes. It's done.

28
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:16,580
We did it, Anne!
Hooray! Great work!

29
00:03:16,670 --> 00:03:18,920
I knew you'd pull through!
Oh, and its look amazing.

30
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,630
[HUGH]
It sounds like a party in here.

31
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:24,250
Let's go. The time's come.

32
00:03:26,330 --> 00:03:28,290
We won't tell
Noah this was a contest.

33
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:32,210
If his pride gets in the way,
he may keep refusing.

34
00:03:33,330 --> 00:03:34,540
[knocks]

35
00:03:35,750 --> 00:03:37,080
[creaks]

36
00:03:37,170 --> 00:03:39,210
Noah. Are you awake?

37
00:03:39,290 --> 00:03:40,380
Huh!

38
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:45,000
[NOAH]
Hmm-uh! Silver Sugar Viscount?

39
00:03:45,670 --> 00:03:47,540
Like I said yesterday,

40
00:03:47,630 --> 00:03:49,580
here's a present
for your kindness.

41
00:03:51,210 --> 00:03:52,290
[gasps]

42
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:55,210
♪

43
00:04:00,130 --> 00:04:01,330
[ANNE]
A fief set.

44
00:04:02,330 --> 00:04:04,000
How did Hugh know about that?

45
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:06,500
So, what do you think?

46
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:09,420
For the board, I figured I could
use the one in the lesser hall.

47
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:10,380
What?

48
00:04:11,170 --> 00:04:14,210
[HUGH] As you know the pieces
were unfortunately lost

49
00:04:14,290 --> 00:04:15,750
when the castle was looted.

50
00:04:15,830 --> 00:04:17,540
However, the Church
of Saint Lewiston Bell

51
00:04:17,630 --> 00:04:20,630
still had some sketches,
so I was able to study those.

52
00:04:20,710 --> 00:04:22,460
Uh-Huh!

53
00:04:23,580 --> 00:04:24,750
Hmm!

54
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:28,630
I also learned your lord
had mastered the game.

55
00:04:28,710 --> 00:04:32,670
Huh! My lord a fief master,
you must be mistaken

56
00:04:32,750 --> 00:04:33,960
he was terrible at it.

57
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:37,500
And that's why no one else
would play it with him.

58
00:04:39,250 --> 00:04:41,420
Oh, well, naturally
they wouldn't.

59
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:45,540
Why would someone challenge him?
The greatest master in the land?

60
00:04:45,630 --> 00:04:47,540
The greatest master?

61
00:04:47,630 --> 00:04:49,290
[gasps]

62
00:04:49,380 --> 00:04:50,960
[HUGH]
But you didn't know that,

63
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:53,500
so you had no problem
asking him to play.

64
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:57,380
I imagine that made
Lord Herbert very happy.

65
00:04:58,210 --> 00:04:59,830
That you wanted a game.

66
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:02,210
Not to compete,
but purely for fun.

67
00:05:02,290 --> 00:05:05,040
♪

68
00:05:06,130 --> 00:05:07,710
So, Lord Herbert.

69
00:05:09,460 --> 00:05:11,210
Do with the pieces as you wish.

70
00:05:12,130 --> 00:05:14,460
They're yours now,
like the old ones.

71
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:16,790
Huh! I see!

72
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:19,750
He might be even more likely to
eat something small like that.

73
00:05:19,830 --> 00:05:21,880
♪

74
00:05:22,670 --> 00:05:24,290
But should I?

75
00:05:26,210 --> 00:05:28,040
[sobs]

76
00:05:35,210 --> 00:05:36,330
Noah,

77
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:39,170
we've brought along another
present for you, as well.

78
00:05:39,250 --> 00:05:42,130
Hm! This belongs to you, too!

79
00:05:43,580 --> 00:05:44,830
Because I made it for you.

80
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:49,500
[gasps]

81
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:51,750
♪

82
00:05:51,830 --> 00:05:53,670
Could it be? Yes!

83
00:05:53,750 --> 00:05:55,710
The crest
of Lord Herbert's house!

84
00:05:55,790 --> 00:05:56,790
This is beautiful!

85
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,250
Like it?

86
00:05:58,330 --> 00:05:59,540
Hmm!

87
00:05:59,630 --> 00:06:00,710
I'm so glad.

88
00:06:00,790 --> 00:06:03,000
[gasps]

89
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:06,080
[ANNE] I hope he can feel,
even if just a little,

90
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:10,540
that the heart of his master
lies in that crest.

91
00:06:10,630 --> 00:06:13,500
♪

92
00:06:34,580 --> 00:06:35,630
[sighs]

93
00:06:36,750 --> 00:06:38,040
[NOAH]
I just ate it.

94
00:06:39,210 --> 00:06:40,250
Did I?

95
00:06:41,830 --> 00:06:43,170
Yes, it's gone!

96
00:06:44,710 --> 00:06:47,170
But I... I was! [sniffles]

97
00:06:47,250 --> 00:06:48,210
[HUGH]
Noah.

98
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:51,130
Here.

99
00:06:51,210 --> 00:06:55,170
♪

100
00:06:57,630 --> 00:06:59,540
I don't understand, sir.

101
00:06:59,630 --> 00:07:01,460
Eat as many as you want.

102
00:07:01,540 --> 00:07:03,580
I can assure you
he won't be angry.

103
00:07:05,250 --> 00:07:08,080
But then I think
you know that, don't you?

104
00:07:08,170 --> 00:07:09,630
[gasps]

105
00:07:09,710 --> 00:07:12,630
[sniffles]

106
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:19,420
If it dwells in your heart,
that crest will never fade.

107
00:07:21,130 --> 00:07:22,670
[NOAH]
Lord Herbert.

108
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:26,580
[sniffles] Whatever they say.

109
00:07:26,670 --> 00:07:28,710
Lord Herbert
truly did live here.

110
00:07:30,170 --> 00:07:34,380
He played fief with me,
ate sugar confections.

111
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:37,170
He was here!
Smiling and having fun!

112
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:39,330
And laughing with me.

113
00:07:39,420 --> 00:07:41,750
[sniffles]

114
00:07:41,830 --> 00:07:45,460
I'll never forget...
the fun we had!

115
00:07:47,710 --> 00:07:49,250
When he was here.

116
00:07:50,210 --> 00:07:54,250
[sniffles]

117
00:07:56,710 --> 00:07:58,210
[HUGH]
That crest has been banned.

118
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:00,920
That confection
that you made him,

119
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,460
it will be seen as
a defiance of the crown.

120
00:08:04,210 --> 00:08:07,040
Didn't you hesitate?
Even for a moment?

121
00:08:07,130 --> 00:08:08,960
You're a silver sugar master!

122
00:08:10,210 --> 00:08:13,080
Just a little but still

123
00:08:13,170 --> 00:08:15,710
I made something that someone
else desperately needed.

124
00:08:16,580 --> 00:08:19,420
If that's so bad, then why even
be a silver sugar master?

125
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:20,710
[gasps]

126
00:08:21,790 --> 00:08:22,790
Hmm!

127
00:08:28,170 --> 00:08:31,040
Of course.
That's why you're a success.

128
00:08:31,130 --> 00:08:32,130
Ah!

129
00:08:32,790 --> 00:08:33,920
[HUGH]
After all.

130
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,330
That crest represents
the spirit of this house.

131
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:38,830
In a way, it serves as proof

132
00:08:38,920 --> 00:08:41,330
that the person
who bore it actually existed.

133
00:08:42,670 --> 00:08:45,080
And Noah's fully aware
of that fact

134
00:08:45,170 --> 00:08:47,880
which is why he sees
his master's heart inside it.

135
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:51,000
But if you understood that

136
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:53,330
then why didn't you make
the crest too?

137
00:08:54,670 --> 00:08:56,380
[HUGH]
I did make it one time.

138
00:08:56,460 --> 00:08:57,580
[gasps]

139
00:08:57,670 --> 00:08:59,380
But I destroyed it.

140
00:08:59,460 --> 00:09:02,960
I'm the Silver Sugar Viscount
and a servant of the crown.

141
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:07,830
That crest is taboo according
to House Millsland

142
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:09,330
and the royal family.

143
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:12,040
So, I dare not depict it.

144
00:09:14,290 --> 00:09:16,170
Tell me something, Hugh.

145
00:09:16,250 --> 00:09:19,170
Why did you become
the Silver Sugar Viscount

146
00:09:19,250 --> 00:09:21,330
if you can only make the pieces
you're told to make?

147
00:09:23,130 --> 00:09:26,960
Hmm! You know something?
Kat asked me that too.

148
00:09:27,750 --> 00:09:29,250
"That power," he said,

149
00:09:29,330 --> 00:09:31,630
"Is it honestly worth giving up
your freedom?"

150
00:09:32,750 --> 00:09:35,080
You should've seen
how angry he was that day.

151
00:09:37,210 --> 00:09:38,500
And the truth is,

152
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:41,960
I did want the power badly
enough to sacrifice freedom.

153
00:09:44,420 --> 00:09:45,790
Because without power,

154
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:48,290
some things
just aren't possible.

155
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:51,330
Confections can be
imbued with prayers,

156
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:53,460
but I needed
something more direct.

157
00:09:55,670 --> 00:09:57,750
Well, that's enough talking.

158
00:09:57,830 --> 00:09:59,790
We've got some important
business.

159
00:10:00,420 --> 00:10:01,790
Go ahead and call him in.

160
00:10:04,210 --> 00:10:08,130
[ANNE] So, if Hugh had made
the crest instead, then...

161
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:14,540
[NADIR]
Hey, Anne!

162
00:10:14,630 --> 00:10:19,130
[laughs] You're amazing!
We found out that you won!

163
00:10:19,210 --> 00:10:20,420
Hmm!

164
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:23,210
I just overheard Elliott talking
with the Silver Sugar Viscount

165
00:10:23,290 --> 00:10:24,750
about it right now!

166
00:10:24,830 --> 00:10:28,380
Which means Mr. Kat is going to
help us finish our work, right?

167
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:30,330
[ELLIOTT]
Precisely!

168
00:10:30,420 --> 00:10:31,880
[ANNE]
Mister Collins.

169
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:33,460
I'll go tell everyone the news!

170
00:10:35,790 --> 00:10:37,130
[ELLIOTT]
The Viscount told me the gist

171
00:10:37,210 --> 00:10:38,420
of how the competition went.

172
00:10:41,630 --> 00:10:43,130
[ANNE]
I don't really think I won.

173
00:10:44,330 --> 00:10:48,540
[chuckles] Well, winner or not,
you solved our problem.

174
00:10:48,630 --> 00:10:49,960
Shouldn't that be enough?

175
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:51,960
Anne. You did it.

176
00:10:53,170 --> 00:10:54,710
Mister Collins.

177
00:10:54,790 --> 00:10:56,710
Anyway! I'll get back to work!

178
00:10:57,630 --> 00:10:59,670
You should go rest for a bit,
Anne.

179
00:10:59,750 --> 00:11:02,000
I'm guessing you probably
stayed up all night worrying.

180
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,580
If that causes you
to make mistakes,

181
00:11:04,670 --> 00:11:06,290
we'll all be in trouble.

182
00:11:06,380 --> 00:11:09,250
Hmm! I'll keep that in mind.

183
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:12,500
Challe!

184
00:11:12,580 --> 00:11:15,420
♪

185
00:11:16,210 --> 00:11:17,960
[CHALLE]
Noah's calmer now.

186
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:20,880
It would appear
your work has helped him a lot.

187
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:23,080
Wonderful!

188
00:11:23,710 --> 00:11:26,040
Hmm! You did well.

189
00:11:26,130 --> 00:11:27,040
[gasps]

190
00:11:28,460 --> 00:11:29,960
Hmm!

191
00:11:31,920 --> 00:11:35,460
♪

192
00:11:41,790 --> 00:11:42,630
[creaks]

193
00:11:42,710 --> 00:11:44,580
Uh! What do you want?

194
00:11:44,670 --> 00:11:46,580
I wasn't just sitting here
staring at them!

195
00:11:46,670 --> 00:11:49,040
♪

196
00:11:49,130 --> 00:11:51,210
[creaks]

197
00:11:53,670 --> 00:11:56,540
[ANNE] Oh. Where's the one
Hugh gave you?

198
00:11:56,630 --> 00:11:58,630
I haven't seen it, so,

199
00:11:58,710 --> 00:12:01,250
I suppose the Viscount
may have wanted it back?

200
00:12:01,330 --> 00:12:02,670
Ha!

201
00:12:02,750 --> 00:12:06,750
Um, but would you mind asking
him if I could keep it, though?

202
00:12:06,830 --> 00:12:09,920
I promise, I would treasure it
for the rest of my life.

203
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:14,040
Really. Do you think
he would give it to me?

204
00:12:14,130 --> 00:12:15,920
Sure. I can ask him.

205
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
It was a gift for you,
after all.

206
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:19,830
- I think he'll say yes.
- Good!

207
00:12:21,380 --> 00:12:24,960
[ANNE] That's odd. I don't see
why he would take it with him.

208
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:28,830
[NOAH] Um. So, your name
isn't thief, it's, uh...

209
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:29,750
I'm Anne.

210
00:12:29,830 --> 00:12:33,460
Right. Tell me, Anne.

211
00:12:33,540 --> 00:12:35,920
Why did you give those
two fairies their wings back?

212
00:12:37,420 --> 00:12:39,170
Is it because they weren't
useful to you?

213
00:12:39,830 --> 00:12:40,830
Noah.

214
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:45,330
Even though Lord Herbert
was so kind, he used to lie.

215
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:49,960
He said that he was bad at fief
when he was a champion.

216
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:52,000
What else was a lie?

217
00:12:53,250 --> 00:12:55,330
Why did he really leave me
behind?

218
00:12:55,420 --> 00:12:58,040
Was it because I was
useless to him, after all?

219
00:12:58,130 --> 00:13:00,170
♪

220
00:13:00,250 --> 00:13:02,170
The reason I gave them back
their wings

221
00:13:02,250 --> 00:13:05,210
is because I see them
the way I see myself.

222
00:13:05,290 --> 00:13:07,000
We're friends,
and we're all equal.

223
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:09,330
So, it's not right
to order them around.

224
00:13:09,420 --> 00:13:10,580
What?

225
00:13:10,670 --> 00:13:12,250
In Lord Herbert's case

226
00:13:12,330 --> 00:13:14,250
maybe, you were that important
to him as well

227
00:13:14,330 --> 00:13:16,290
and that's why he set you free.

228
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:18,040
He cared about you very much.

229
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:21,210
Uh-huh!
Do you really think that was it?

230
00:13:22,330 --> 00:13:24,710
Mmm-hmm! And he adored you.

231
00:13:27,750 --> 00:13:30,250
Now then, why not rest
a little while,

232
00:13:30,330 --> 00:13:32,750
if you do then you will
have even more energy!

233
00:13:32,830 --> 00:13:34,000
[NOAH]
All right.

234
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:36,710
♪

235
00:13:37,580 --> 00:13:42,170
Anne, stay here and hold my hand
until I fall asleep, would you?

236
00:13:42,250 --> 00:13:43,130
I will.

237
00:13:43,210 --> 00:13:44,380
[sighs]

238
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:48,330
♪

239
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:59,040
[HERBERT] I'm grateful.
Silver Sugar Master.

240
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:02,630
Because of you,
I too can leave this castle

241
00:14:02,710 --> 00:14:03,830
with a peaceful heart.

242
00:14:05,540 --> 00:14:07,000
At long last.

243
00:14:08,790 --> 00:14:09,710
[ANNE]
Lord Herbert.

244
00:14:11,250 --> 00:14:13,380
For this year's Pull Soul Day,

245
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:15,330
I'll make a sugar confection
in your honor.

246
00:14:16,630 --> 00:14:19,210
And then,
I know you'll make it to heaven.

247
00:14:21,330 --> 00:14:23,920
[ORLAND] Now we can finally do
the assembly work we put off.

248
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:26,210
Right! Anne saved the day!

249
00:14:26,290 --> 00:14:28,710
You know. Anne made him a crest

250
00:14:28,790 --> 00:14:30,460
and it was even better
than the fief set

251
00:14:30,540 --> 00:14:31,750
that the Viscount made!

252
00:14:31,830 --> 00:14:34,040
I wish I could have seen
his work for myself.

253
00:14:34,130 --> 00:14:34,960
Would be an honor.

254
00:14:35,670 --> 00:14:37,040
So, she did win.

255
00:14:41,830 --> 00:14:42,830
Where's Gladus?

256
00:14:45,290 --> 00:14:46,670
[creaks]

257
00:14:46,750 --> 00:14:49,460
Are you here, Gladus? It's me.

258
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:53,500
[footsteps]

259
00:14:57,380 --> 00:14:58,380
What are you doing?

260
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:01,920
Huh!

261
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:05,210
♪

262
00:15:05,290 --> 00:15:06,380
Isn't that?

263
00:15:06,460 --> 00:15:08,290
Oh, it's just you.

264
00:15:09,250 --> 00:15:10,580
[BRIDGET]
Wait, don't eat that!

265
00:15:10,670 --> 00:15:13,040
It was crafted for that child
fairy who was starving!

266
00:15:14,040 --> 00:15:15,750
It's to bring him happiness!

267
00:15:16,710 --> 00:15:18,830
He's the only one
who's permitted to have it!

268
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:21,960
You have no business
laying your hands on it!

269
00:15:23,830 --> 00:15:25,380
[gasps]

270
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:26,710
Be quiet.

271
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:29,630
[sighs] No!

272
00:15:29,710 --> 00:15:31,420
[groans]

273
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:38,880
It's giving me so much power!

274
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:42,830
I'd expect nothing less
from the Viscount. How lovely.

275
00:15:43,960 --> 00:15:45,330
[BRIDGET]
Why?

276
00:15:45,420 --> 00:15:46,290
[LAFALLE]
I was injured.

277
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:48,880
It took a while to find
something strong enough

278
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:49,920
to restore me.

279
00:15:51,130 --> 00:15:53,500
So, imagine
my luck finding these.

280
00:15:54,170 --> 00:15:55,790
[BRIDGET]
You used me, didn't you?

281
00:15:55,880 --> 00:15:58,710
[LAFALLE] Indeed, and it
gives me no joy to admit this,

282
00:15:58,790 --> 00:16:01,130
but I didn't feel
even a speck of guilt.

283
00:16:02,540 --> 00:16:04,330
[sighs]

284
00:16:04,420 --> 00:16:06,080
- Oh, what now?
- I think you know!

285
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:10,460
♪

286
00:16:10,540 --> 00:16:11,580
Ah!

287
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:14,750
[chuckles]

288
00:16:14,830 --> 00:16:16,040
But why?

289
00:16:16,130 --> 00:16:18,000
[LAFALLE]
Well, that was cruel.

290
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:21,580
Whoever owns that wing must be
in terrible agony right now.

291
00:16:21,670 --> 00:16:23,330
[BRIDGET]
[gasps] Stay back!

292
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:25,830
[exhales]

293
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:29,500
Don't interrupt my meal.

294
00:16:32,540 --> 00:16:36,040
[footsteps]

295
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:41,130
[LAFALLE]
Found you at last. Brooding?

296
00:16:42,290 --> 00:16:43,580
Tell me honestly!

297
00:16:43,670 --> 00:16:45,580
Why do you desire
to get close to me?

298
00:16:46,830 --> 00:16:48,170
What lovely eyes.

299
00:16:48,250 --> 00:16:49,710
Be serious.

300
00:16:49,790 --> 00:16:51,790
Oh, I am serious.

301
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:54,790
It's something
that I've envisioned endlessly.

302
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:56,880
I knew that
the obsidian fairy's eyes

303
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:58,540
would be incomparably beautiful.

304
00:17:00,290 --> 00:17:02,040
Challe fenn Challe.

305
00:17:02,130 --> 00:17:05,290
As soon as I heard your name,
there could be no doubt.

306
00:17:05,380 --> 00:17:07,790
I was certain that I'd found
someone I had been seeking

307
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:09,170
for quite a long time.

308
00:17:10,250 --> 00:17:11,830
I never knew your face or name.

309
00:17:12,580 --> 00:17:14,960
The only thing I knew was
that you had been born.

310
00:17:16,500 --> 00:17:19,000
Through unfortunate coincidence,

311
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:21,460
we two were torn
from each other.

312
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:23,580
I feared that we may never meet.

313
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:26,750
Then I gave up hope,
and a century passed.

314
00:17:27,790 --> 00:17:29,130
But now, we're together!

315
00:17:29,960 --> 00:17:33,670
Who are you?
Tell me what your true name is.

316
00:17:33,750 --> 00:17:37,000
I'm so happy you asked.
Lafalle fenn Lafalle.

317
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:38,580
[gasps]

318
00:17:38,670 --> 00:17:40,460
Lafalle fenn Lafalle?

319
00:17:40,540 --> 00:17:41,920
What's wrong?

320
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,750
It ought to sound familiar
to you, Shall.

321
00:17:44,830 --> 00:17:46,790
Since the moment
that you were born

322
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:50,210
it has been ringing out
from deep inside your very soul.

323
00:17:50,290 --> 00:17:53,290
The stone that bore me was set
into the hilt of a sword

324
00:17:53,380 --> 00:17:55,170
forgotten to time.

325
00:17:55,250 --> 00:17:56,790
[LAFALLE]
That's right.

326
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:59,380
A sword enshrined within a
darkened chapel,

327
00:17:59,460 --> 00:18:00,790
as though to hide it.

328
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:03,040
As you know there was an opal

329
00:18:03,130 --> 00:18:05,540
and a diamond embedded
into the hilt as well.

330
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:10,000
I am the fairy who came
from that opal

331
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:12,670
before the obsidian spawned you.

332
00:18:12,750 --> 00:18:15,330
Those three precious stones
were chosen specifically,

333
00:18:15,420 --> 00:18:17,670
with the hope that something
would be born out of them.

334
00:18:18,290 --> 00:18:22,040
By whom?
Who was the one responsible?

335
00:18:22,130 --> 00:18:23,630
Why the sword's master.

336
00:18:23,710 --> 00:18:25,790
You tell me who it was,
immediately!

337
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:27,830
There's no need to rush.

338
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:31,880
For at the appropriate moment,
I'll happily explain everything.

339
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:34,750
What you've asked me
and what you've yet to wonder.

340
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,710
Challe, you must come with me.

341
00:18:38,790 --> 00:18:40,750
You and I are meant to be
together.

342
00:18:40,830 --> 00:18:42,880
Our destiny is predetermined.

343
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:46,460
The fact we've reunited after
a hundred years should be proof.

344
00:18:46,540 --> 00:18:48,210
[CHALLE]
What did you say?

345
00:18:48,290 --> 00:18:50,380
Free yourself
from humanity's control!

346
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:53,210
Come away with me!

347
00:18:53,290 --> 00:18:57,500
♪

348
00:19:02,380 --> 00:19:05,290
My fate will
not be decided by you!

349
00:19:05,380 --> 00:19:07,710
I had a feeling you'd say that.

350
00:19:07,790 --> 00:19:11,130
Perhaps if I obtained that girl,
you might be more cooperative.

351
00:19:11,210 --> 00:19:12,290
[CHALLE]
I won't let you have her!

352
00:19:12,380 --> 00:19:14,880
[LAFALLE]
Let me? You can't stop me!

353
00:19:17,170 --> 00:19:18,040
Huh!

354
00:19:21,210 --> 00:19:22,710
So, that was you.

355
00:19:22,790 --> 00:19:25,790
[LAFALLE] I'll admit, the cut
you gave me had quite an effect

356
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:28,420
but now, thanks
to the Silver Sugar Viscount's

357
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:31,500
confections,
I'm feeling better than ever.

358
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:34,460
You're bold to reveal your true
identity to me.

359
00:19:34,540 --> 00:19:35,960
Just don't run away this time.

360
00:19:37,080 --> 00:19:39,250
Well, this is a problem.

361
00:19:39,330 --> 00:19:40,710
You see, my original intention

362
00:19:40,790 --> 00:19:43,380
was to slice you into ribbons
on the spot,

363
00:19:43,460 --> 00:19:44,920
but things have changed now.

364
00:19:45,540 --> 00:19:47,880
Since I don't desire
to hurt you.

365
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:50,580
I am at a staggering
disadvantage.

366
00:19:50,670 --> 00:19:52,380
So, to even the odds a bit.

367
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:55,130
♪

368
00:19:55,210 --> 00:19:56,790
I will be taking the girl.

369
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:57,750
Urgh!

370
00:19:58,580 --> 00:20:01,500
[LAFALLE] That way, you'll
belong to me as well, yes?

371
00:20:12,380 --> 00:20:14,710
She's going to be mine.

372
00:20:14,790 --> 00:20:17,080
[laughs]

373
00:20:17,170 --> 00:20:21,080
Resist all you like
my fate is bound to yours.

374
00:20:23,630 --> 00:20:24,750
Huh!

375
00:20:27,210 --> 00:20:28,630
Anne!

376
00:20:28,710 --> 00:20:29,960
[door opens]

377
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:33,830
♪

378
00:20:35,130 --> 00:20:38,040
Hmm! Challe? What's wrong?

379
00:20:40,630 --> 00:20:42,040
[gasps]

380
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:44,540
I won't let you go.

381
00:20:46,750 --> 00:20:48,420
[ANNE]
What happened?

382
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:49,880
No one will take you.

383
00:20:50,580 --> 00:20:53,670
I gave you my word.
I will protect you.

384
00:20:53,750 --> 00:20:57,630
♪

